<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Cockburn, Melville and Canning cover a big slice of the southern suburbs: the ABS counted 139,499 people in Cockburn, 115,945 in Melville and 109,028 in Canning in mid-2025. The calls from here tend to be everyday ones: a wall coming out for an open-plan kitchen, a crack that wasn't there last summer, an extension the building surveyor wants engineered, or a patio that needs a certificate before the permit is issued.</p><p>Kings Park Structural Co is a referral service, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to an independent structural engineering firm, which pays us for the introduction and quotes and contracts with you directly. Sometimes the honest first answer is that you don't need an engineer at all, and we'd rather you knew that before you spend money.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Cockburn, Melville & Canning</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Cockburn, Melville & Canning Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Wall removal and beam design</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">WA is the only state where more than half of detached houses are brick, and in a double-brick house internal walls often carry the ceiling and roof. An independent engineer checks the wall and designs the beam before a builder in Cockburn, Melville or Canning touches it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Crack and structural reports</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For owners worried about cracks in brickwork, render or ceilings, or who need an independent report for a purchase, a builder dispute or an insurer. It's an engineer's assessment, which is a different thing from a pre-purchase building inspection.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Extension and second-storey engineering</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Any change to floor area or height needs a building permit, and the building surveyor will want engineering for footings, beams and any new load on existing walls. The engineer quotes once they've seen your plans.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Patio, carport and shed certificates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A roofed patio isn't a pergola under the WA exemptions, so most patios and carports need a permit. An engineer's certificate covers the design, the wind loading and the footings for your particular block.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
